  '["A warehouse scanner reports a list of package weights. Given a target weight, decide whether two different packages in the list weigh exactly the target together.","The two packages must be at different positions in the list. They may have the same weight, but a single package cannot be used twice."]'::jsonb, '["The first line contains two integers `n` and `target`.","The second line contains `n` integers `a[0] … a[n-1]`, separated by spaces."]'::jsonb, '["Print `YES` if there are indices `i ≠ j` with `a[i] + a[j] = target`. Otherwise print `NO`."]'::jsonb, '["2 ≤ n ≤ 40000","-10^9 ≤ a[i] ≤ 10^9","-10^9 ≤ target ≤ 10^9","A sum of two values can reach ±2·10^9, which overflows a signed 32-bit integer. Python integers and JavaScript numbers represent it exactly."]'::jsonb,
